    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n28041" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Mărĭandȳni</span></b> ,
			ōrum, m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Μαριανδυνοί</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a people of Bithynia</i>, <i><span class="en">Mel. 1, 19,
				1</span></i>; <i><span class="en">7</span></i>; <i><span class="en">2, 7, 2</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Val. Fl. 4,
				171</span></i>; Avien. Descr. Orbis, 960; <i><span class="en">Mart.
				Cap. 9, § 924</span></i>.—Hence, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Mărĭ-andȳnus</span></b> , a,
				um, <i>adj., of</i> or <i>belonging to the Mariandyni, Mariandynian</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sinus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin. 6,
					1, 1, § 4</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">arenae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Val.
					Fl. 4, 733</span></i>
			.</div>
